INT. COLLAPSED MINE ELEVATOR CAGE - NIGHT

A steel cage wedged in a vertical shaft, tilted twenty degrees, hanging by a single frayed cable. Pebbles tick down from above. A dim headlamp illuminates two men and a bucket of water.

DESMOND "DEZ" HOLLOWAY, forties, a foreman with a broken arm in a makeshift sling, sits against the bars. ARCHIE PENHALIGON, twenties, a fresh-faced miner with a bleeding scalp, crouches on the opposite side, rope looped round his wrist.

DEZ
Archie, kid, how's your head?

ARCHIE
It's fine, Dez.

DEZ
It's not fine. I can see it from here.

ARCHIE
Then don't look.

Dez shifts. The cage groans. The cable above pings like a plucked string. Both men go perfectly still.

DEZ
Don't breathe.

ARCHIE
I'm not breathing.

DEZ
Good man.

They hold. The cage settles. Dez lets out a ragged breath.

DEZ (CONT'D)
Okay. Okay. We're okay.

ARCHIE
Dez, how long have we been down here?

DEZ
Nine hours.

ARCHIE
They'd have come by now.

DEZ
They'll come.

ARCHIE
Dez. Nobody's coming.

Dez does not answer. He looks at his arm. He looks at the water bucket. He looks at Archie.

DEZ
Archie, you're the lightest. If you climb the cable, you can reach the ladder.

ARCHIE
Climb it?

DEZ
It's twenty feet. You've done worse.

ARCHIE
I've never done worse.

DEZ
Archie.

ARCHIE
He'll cut me loose, Dez. The cable. It won't take two.

DEZ
Then it won't take one either. It'll take whatever it takes.

Archie loops the rope around his waist. He tests the knot. His hands shake.

ARCHIE
Hold the rope.

DEZ
I've got you.

He rises. Dez wraps the rope around his good arm. Archie reaches for the cable, grips it, lifts one boot. The cage swings.

DEZ (CONT'D)
Easy! Easy, kid!

ARCHIE
I'm easy!

He climbs. Three feet. Five. The cable twangs. A strand parts, then another, curling like wire hair. Dez cries out. Archie stops.

ARCHIE (CONT'D)
Dez, it's going!

DEZ
Keep climbing!

ARCHIE
It's going, Dez!

DEZ
Do not stop, Archie! Do not stop!

Archie lunges. His fingers catch a rung. The cage drops six inches with a scream of metal. Dez is flung against the bars. The rope snaps taut on his arm and he roars through his teeth.

DEZ (CONT'D)
Go! Go!

Archie pulls himself onto the ladder. He turns, hanging there, breathing like a bellows, and stares down at Dez.

ARCHIE
I'm on, Dez. I'm on!

DEZ
(weak laugh)
Of course you are.

The cable parts with a crack like a gunshot. The cage falls away into the dark and its crash echoes up the shaft, long after it has gone.

ARCHIE
(whisper)
Dez?

Nothing. Then, from impossibly far below, a faint voice.

DEZ (O.S.)
Climb, Archie.
